{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A53RLDNnitQ92LFEAWzaku","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Configure Phoenix JSON encoder\n     2→Application.put_env(:phoenix, :json_library, Jason)\n     3→\n     4→# Configure the test endpoint\n     5→Application.put_env(:live_vite, LiveVite.E2E.Endpoint,\n     6→  http: [ip: {127, 0, 0, 1}, port: 4004],\n     7→  adapter: Bandit.PhoenixAdapter,\n     8→  server: true,\n     9→  live_view: [signing_salt: \"aaaaaaaa\"],\n    10→  secret_key_base: String.duplicate(\"a\", 64),\n    11→  check_origin: false,\n    12→  debug_errors: true,\n    13→  code_reloader: true,\n    14→  pubsub_server: LiveVite.E2E.PubSub,\n    15→  reloadable_apps: [:live_vite],\n    16→  live_reload: [\n    17→    patterns: [\n    18→      ~r\"lib/live_vite/.*(ex|exs)$\",\n    19→      ~r\"test/e2e/features/.*\\.(ex|exs|vue|js|ts|tsx|jsx)$\"\n    20→    ]\n    21→  ]\n    22→)\n    23→\n    24→Application.put_env(:live_vite, :enable_props_diff, true)\n    25→Application.put_env(:live_vite, :ssr_default, false)\n    26→\n    27→Process.register(self(), :e2e_helper)\n    28→\n    29→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.ErrorHTML do\n    30→  def render(template, _), do: Phoenix.Controller.status_message_from_template(template)\n    31→end\n    32→\n    33→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.Layout do\n    34→  @moduledoc false\n    35→  use Phoenix.Component\n    36→\n    37→  def render(\"root.html\", assigns) do\n    38→    ~H\"\"\"\n    39→    <!DOCTYPE html>\n    40→    <html>\n    41→      <head>\n    42→        <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    43→        <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    44→        <meta name=\"csrf-token\" content={Plug.CSRFProtection.get_csrf_token()} />\n    45→        <title>LiveVite E2E</title>\n    46→      </head>\n    47→      <body>\n    48→        {@inner_content}\n    49→      </body>\n    50→    </html>\n    51→    \"\"\"\n    52→  end\n    53→\n    54→  def render(\"live.html\", assigns) do\n    55→    ~H\"\"\"\n    56→    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/assets/app.js\">\n    57→    </script>\n    58→    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/assets/app.css\" />\n    59→    {@inner_content}\n    60→    \"\"\"\n    61→  end\n    62→end\n    63→\n    64→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.Hooks do\n    65→  @moduledoc false\n    66→  import Phoenix.LiveView\n    67→\n    68→  alias Phoenix.LiveView.Socket\n    69→\n    70→  require Logger\n    71→\n    72→  def on_mount(:default, _params, _session, socket) do\n    73→    socket\n    74→    |> attach_hook(:eval_handler, :handle_event, &handle_eval_event/3)\n    75→    |> then(&{:cont, &1})\n    76→  end\n    77→\n    78→  defp handle_eval_event(\"sandbox:eval\", %{\"value\" => code}, socket) do\n    79→    {result, _} = Code.eval_string(code, [socket: socket], __ENV__)\n    80→    Logger.debug(\"lv:#{inspect(self())} eval result: #{inspect(result)}\")\n    81→\n    82→    case result do\n    83→      {:noreply, %Socket{} = socket} -> {:halt, %{}, socket}\n    84→      %Socket{} = socket -> {:halt, %{}, socket}\n    85→      result -> {:halt, %{\"result\" => result}, socket}\n    86→    end\n    87→  end\n    88→\n    89→  defp handle_eval_event(_, _, socket), do: {:cont, socket}\n    90→end\n    91→\n    92→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.HealthController do\n    93→  import Plug.Conn\n    94→\n    95→  def init(opts), do: opts\n    96→\n    97→  def index(conn, _params) do\n    98→    send_resp(conn, 200, \"OK\")\n    99→  end\n   100→end\n   101→\n   102→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.Router do\n   103→  use Phoenix.Router\n   104→\n   105→  import Phoenix.LiveView.Router\n   106→\n   107→  alias LiveVite.E2E.Layout\n   108→\n   109→  pipeline :browser do\n   110→    plug :accepts, [\"html\"]\n   111→    plug :fetch_session\n   112→    plug :fetch_live_flash\n   113→    plug :protect_from_forgery\n   114→    plug :put_root_layout, html: {Layout, :root}\n   115→  end\n   116→\n   117→  live_session :default,\n   118→    layout: {Layout, :live},\n   119→    on_mount: {LiveVite.E2E.Hooks, :default} do\n   120→    scope \"/\", LiveVite.E2E do\n   121→      pipe_through(:browser)\n   122→\n   123→      live \"/test\", TestLive\n   124→      live \"/prop-diff-test\", PropDiffTestLive\n   125→      live \"/navigation/:page\", NavigationLive\n   126→      live \"/navigation/alt/:page\", NavigationLive\n   127→      live \"/events\", EventLive\n   128→      live \"/upload/:mode\", UploadTestLive\n   129→      live \"/streams\", StreamLive\n   130→      live \"/form-test\", FormTestLive\n   131→      live \"/event-reply-test\", EventReplyTestLive\n   132→      live \"/slot-test\", SlotTestLive\n   133→      live \"/memory-benchmark\", MemoryBenchmarkLive\n   134→\n   135→      # React E2E test routes\n   136→      live \"/react-test\", ReactTestLive\n   137→      live \"/react-prop-diff-test\", ReactPropDiffTestLive\n   138→      live \"/react-navigation/:page\", ReactNavigationLive\n   139→      live \"/react-navigation/alt/:page\", ReactNavigationLive\n   140→      live \"/react-events\", ReactEventLive\n   141→      live \"/react-streams\", ReactStreamLive\n   142→      live \"/react-slot-test\", ReactSlotTestLive\n   143→    end\n   144→  end\n   145→\n   146→  scope \"/\", LiveVite.E2E do\n   147→    pipe_through(:browser)\n   148→\n   149→    get \"/health\", HealthController, :index\n   150→    get \"/dead-view\", DeadViewController, :show\n   151→  end\n   152→end\n   153→\n   154→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.Endpoint do\n   155→  use Phoenix.Endpoint, otp_app: :live_vite\n   156→\n   157→  @session_options [\n   158→    store: :cookie,\n   159→    key: \"_lv_e2e_key\",\n   160→    signing_salt: \"aaaaaaaa\",\n   161→    same_site: \"Lax\"\n   162→  ]\n   163→\n   164→  socket \"/live\", Phoenix.LiveView.Socket, websocket: [connect_info: [session: @session_options]]\n   165→\n   166→  # Code reloading configuration\n   167→  if code_reloading? do\n   168→    socket \"/phoenix/live_reload/socket\", Phoenix.LiveReloader.Socket\n   169→    plug Phoenix.LiveReloader\n   170→    plug Phoenix.CodeReloader\n   171→  end\n   172→\n   173→  plug Plug.Static, from: {:phoenix, \"priv/static\"}, at: \"/assets/phoenix\"\n   174→  plug Plug.Static, from: {:phoenix_live_view, \"priv/static\"}, at: \"/assets/phoenix_live_view\"\n   175→  plug Plug.Static, from: \"test/e2e/priv/static/assets\", at: \"/assets\"\n   176→\n   177→  plug :health_check\n   178→  plug :halt\n   179→\n   180→  plug Plug.Parsers,\n   181→    parsers: [:urlencoded, :multipart, :json],\n   182→    pass: [\"*/*\"],\n   183→    json_decoder: Phoenix.json_library()\n   184→\n   185→  plug Plug.Session, @session_options\n   186→  plug LiveVite.E2E.Router\n   187→\n   188→  defp health_check(%{request_path: \"/health\"} = conn, _opts) do\n   189→    conn\n   190→    |> Plug.Conn.send_resp(200, \"OK\")\n   191→    |> Plug.Conn.halt()\n   192→  end\n   193→\n   194→  defp health_check(conn, _opts), do: conn\n   195→\n   196→  defp halt(%{request_path: \"/halt\"}, _opts) do\n   197→    send(:e2e_helper, :halt)\n   198→    Process.sleep(:infinity)\n   199→  end\n   200→\n   201→  defp halt(conn, _opts), do: conn\n   202→end\n   203→\n   204→# Start PubSub and Endpoint\n   205→# Note: LiveView modules are compiled from test/e2e/features/*/live.ex via elixirc_paths in mix.exs\n   206→{:ok, _} =\n   207→  Supervisor.start_link(\n   208→    [\n   209→      LiveVite.E2E.Endpoint,\n   210→      {Phoenix.PubSub, name: LiveVite.E2E.PubSub}\n   211→    ],\n   212→    strategy: :one_for_one\n   213→  )\n   214→\n   215→IO.puts(\"Starting e2e server on port #{LiveVite.E2E.Endpoint.config(:http)[:port]}\")\n   216→\n   217→if not IEx.started?() do\n   218→  spawn(fn ->\n   219→    IO.read(:stdio, :line)\n   220→    send(:e2e_helper, :halt)\n   221→  end)\n   222→\n   223→  receive do\n   224→    :halt -> :ok\n   225→  end\n   226→end\n   227→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiCBZP9CP3dkzuNW4JLfaX","session_id":"8cfcad3f-3a06-41f0-92cb-a7a9566506cd","uuid":"0361a4a6-bc2c-481c-817a-0109c4359a5c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiCBZP9CP3dkzuNW4JLfaX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the full content of `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/test_helper.exs` with analysis of the three items you requested:\n\n## 1. Route Registration Pattern (lines 117-144)\n\nRoutes are registered within a `live_session :default` block that sets up:\n- Layout: `{Layout, :live}` - provides the live layout template with module/component loading\n- On-mount hook: `{LiveVite.E2E.Hooks, :default}` - attaches the eval handler for sandbox eval operations\n\nAll routes fall under `scope \"/\", LiveVite.E2E` which maps to the `LiveVite.E2E` module namespace.\n\n## 2. React-Specific Routes (lines 135-142)\n\nReact routes follow a clear naming convention with the `react-` prefix:\n- `/react-test` → `ReactTestLive`\n- `/react-prop-diff-test` → `ReactPropDiffTestLive`\n- `/react-navigation/:page` → `ReactNavigationLive`\n- `/react-navigation/alt/:page` → `ReactNavigationLive` (same as above)\n- `/react-events` → `ReactEventLive`\n- `/react-streams` → `ReactStreamLive`\n- `/react-slot-test` → `ReactSlotTestLive`\n\nEach maps to a corresponding `React*Live` LiveView module in the `LiveVite.E2E` namespace.\n\n## 3. Component Registration/Resolve Patterns\n\nThe file doesn't contain explicit component resolution code. However, there are key clues:\n- Line 19: The live_reload patterns include `.tsx` and `.jsx` files, indicating React component support\n- Line 205: A comment states \"LiveView modules are compiled from `test/e2e/features/*/live.ex` via elixirc_paths in mix.exs\"\n- This suggests component resolution happens dynamically through the LiveView modules themselves (in the individual `live.ex` files for each feature)\n\nThe actual component registration/resolve patterns would be in the individual `test/e2e/features/*/live.ex` files that define each `ReactTestLive`, `ReactEventLive`, etc. module."},{"type